N00B_DIAG(OUTPUT_NOT_WRITABLE, "N00B-B0100", ERROR,
    "an output file cannot be written",
    "The compiler writes the executable (or other output) to the path given\n"
    "with `--output`, or next to the input by default. The message names the\n"
    "path and the reason the operating system gave: a directory that does\n"
    "not exist, missing permission, or a directory where a file should go.")
N00B_DIAG(LINKER_NOT_FOUND, "N00B-B0101", ERROR,
    "there is no linker to build the executable with",
    "n00b links executables with clang. Install LLVM, or set N00B_CLANG to\n"
    "a clang executable. `n00b env` shows which clang this toolchain uses.")
N00B_DIAG(LINKER_START_FAILED, "N00B-B0102", ERROR,
    "the linker cannot be started",
    "The linker named in the message exists in the configuration but could\n"
    "not run. Check N00B_CLANG, or reinstall LLVM; `n00b env` shows the\n"
    "linker this toolchain uses.")
N00B_DIAG(UNDEFINED_NATIVE_SYMBOL, "N00B-B0103", ERROR,
    "the program calls a native function that nothing being linked defines",
    "A foreign function declared in an 'ffi literal must be supplied by a\n"
    "native library or object at link time. Name the library in the 'ffi\n"
    "literal, or pass the object or archive that defines it with\n"
    "`--link-object <file>`.")
N00B_DIAG(LINK_FAILED, "N00B-B0104", ERROR,
    "the linker fails to produce the executable",
    "The linker reported an error other than a missing symbol, or stopped\n"
    "abnormally. Its output and the full link command are shown as notes.")
N00B_DIAG(START_SIGNATURE, "N00B-B0105", ERROR,
    "the program's `start` function has the wrong signature",
    "An executable begins at `start` in the root module, which takes no\n"
    "parameters and returns nothing:\n"
    "    func start() -> nil {\n"
    "    }\n"
    "Report failure by raising or panicking rather than returning a value.")
N00B_DIAG(RUNTIME_LIBRARY_MISSING, "N00B-B0106", ERROR,
    "the n00b runtime library is missing from the toolchain",
    "Every executable links against the runtime library that ships with the\n"
    "toolchain. It was not found where `n00b env` says it should be;\n"
    "reinstall the toolchain, or rebuild the checkout.")
N00B_DIAG(SAME_MODULE_TWO_FILES, "N00B-N1500", ERROR,
    "one module name resolves to two different files",
    "Every module name must identify exactly one source file. Two package\n"
    "roots (the current directory, N00B_PATH entries, the standard library)\n"
    "can each hold a file for the same name; remove or rename one copy.")
N00B_DIAG(CONFLICTING_DECLARATIONS, "N00B-N1502", ERROR,
    "two declarations of one name disagree",
    "Declarations of the same name in a module must agree on what kind of\n"
    "thing it is, its visibility and its signature. The message names the\n"
    "property that differs.")
N00B_DIAG(UNRESOLVED_DECLARATION, "N00B-N1503", ERROR,
    "a use refers to a name that no module in the program provides",
    "The name was expected in the module shown, but nothing linked into the\n"
    "program declares it. Check the module's exports, or link the\n"
    "interface that provides it.")
N00B_DIAG(MODULE_SUPPLIED_TWICE, "N00B-N1504", ERROR,
    "a module is supplied to the build twice",
    "A module can come from source or from a linked interface\n"
    "(`--link-interface`), but only once.")
N00B_DIAG(STALE_DESCRIPTION, "N00B-N1505", ERROR,
    "a module description was written by a different compiler version",
    "Linked interfaces and cached build products carry a format version.\n"
    "Rebuild the interface with this compiler, or run `n00b cache clean`.")
N00B_DIAG(NATIVE_LIBRARY_MISSING, "N00B-F0001", ERROR,
    "a native library named by an 'ffi literal cannot be found",
    "The linker could not find the library the 'ffi literal asks for. Install\n"
    "it, or add its directory to the literal's search paths so the linker can\n"
    "find it.")
N00B_DIAG(RUST_TRANSPORT_UNAVAILABLE, "N00B-F0002", ERROR,
    "an 'ffi literal needs Rust transports, which this n00b was built without",
    "Some foreign interfaces are reached through a generated Rust crate.\n"
    "Rebuild n00b with N00B_RUST=1 to enable them.")
N00B_DIAG(TRANSPORT_CACHE_UNAVAILABLE, "N00B-F0003", ERROR,
    "there is no cache directory to build an 'ffi literal's Rust crate in",
    "The generated Rust crate is built and kept in the n00b cache. Set\n"
    "N00B_CACHE to a writable directory.")
N00B_DIAG(TRANSPORT_BUILD_FAILED, "N00B-F0004", ERROR,
    "the Rust crate generated for an 'ffi literal fails to build",
    "cargo could not build the transport crate. The message names the log\n"
    "with cargo's output; the usual causes are a missing Rust toolchain or a\n"
    "network failure while fetching dependencies.")
N00B_DIAG(SHIM_COMPILE_FAILED, "N00B-F0005", ERROR,
    "the C code generated for an 'ffi literal fails to compile",
    "Foreign calls go through small C shims compiled with clang against the\n"
    "headers the 'ffi literal names. The headers must be found and must\n"
    "declare what the literal describes; clang's own messages are printed\n"
    "just before this one.")
N00B_DIAG(PROVIDED_FUNCTION_MISSING, "N00B-F0006", ERROR,
    "an 'ffi binding provides a function that does not exist",
    "A `provide` line in an 'ffi binding names the n00b function that\n"
    "implements a callback, as `module.function`. That function must exist\n"
    "and have a body:\n"
    "    provide nth_sorted.compare = \"sorting.descending\"")
N00B_DIAG(NATIVE_ROOT_MISSING, "N00B-B0107", ERROR,
    "`--native-root` names a function that does not exist",
    "`--native-root NAME=module.function` exports an existing n00b\n"
    "function under a C symbol name. The function must exist in the\n"
    "program and have a body.")
N00B_DIAG(LINKER_WARNING, "N00B-B0108", WARNING,
    "the linker warns about the executable it produced",
    "The link succeeded, but the linker printed a warning, often about a\n"
    "native library built for a different platform version or a duplicate\n"
    "library on the link line. The linker's text is shown as the message.")
